Edits (power the VM off first, then edit the .vmx):

mks.enable3d = "FALSE"
svga.graphicsMemoryKB = "262144"
sata0:1.present = "FALSE"
sound.present = "FALSE"
sound.autoDetect = "FALSE"
usb.vbluetooth.startConnected = "FALSE"
serial0.present = "FALSE"
msg.autoAnswer = "TRUE"

On shares2, also add numvcpus = "2". msg.autoAnswer makes the VM answer any question dialog automatically, which is what an unattended start needs.

For vm-watchdog.ps1, set $vms to the real paths. For shares I’m assuming the file is G:\shares.vmx, since you gave the folder as G:\:

"G:\shares.vmx"
"G:\Virtual Machines\shares2\shares2.vmx"

Each host’s watchdog should list only the VM that runs on that host.
